{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's perception and actuation capabilities, separating sensing (uncontrollable events) from motion (controllable events). The specification enforces safe, coverage-oriented exploration: in clear states, random_walk is preferred for coverage; after obstacle detection, the robot executes a short, directed recovery turn (direction chosen to avoid blocked sides), then returns to exploration as soon as the path is clear. Full_rotate is reserved for rare, persistent blockage. All transitions are deterministic, and the supervisor avoids oscillations and overuse of recovery.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for sensing and motion to reflect the robot's hardware interface.",
    "Specification automaton encodes safe, coverage-biased exploration: random_walk in clear, move_forward for short progress, directed turn recovery on obstacle, and rare full_rotate as last resort."
  ],
